WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
joining me now  the former democrat state senate leader  who's endorsing larry elder gloria  ramirez gloria it's an honor to have you  on this program tonight  i have to ask thank you thank you  um why was education the breaking point  for you  my mother had a sixth grade level of  education i earned a phd and ultimately  chaired the senate education committee  to me education is a civil rights issue  and especially in california with over  six million children in the public  school system i take a look at the  outcomes and we find that some seventy  percent of latino children cannot do  math at grade level standards it's about  80 percent for african-american youth  and that was before the pandemic and now  they're trying to teach our youth that  four you know that two plus two doesn't  even equal four to me i believe that  school choice is what breaks the chains  of poverty and i finally got tired of  waiting for governor after governor  legislature after legislature to do  something right for especially children  of color but really all children all  families in california that's why i  gravitated to support the recall and  especially larry elder you know school  choice broke the cycle for me and my  family but i got to ask you  what happens  if gavin newsom remains the governor  well again two what happens is we're  going to see same old same old  essentially sadly and i'm a democrat i  have personally seen the hostage taking  the political hostage taking in  sacramento i have seen personally  whether it's by the humongous campaign  contributions the outsized influence of  how policy is written basically no  budget gets decided without the input of  the cta the california teachers  association so what happens is basically  it's like groundhog day except when it  comes to our school children it's a very  serious negative effect as a democrat i  really am disappointed in a democratic  party that purports to stand for  the rights of minorities of working  class communities and yet it fails on  the most important issue for us  education so i think the schools will be  shut down again we're going to continue  to see the captive audience to special  interests that run the show in  sacramento gavin will be fine his kids  will continue to go to the private  school of his choice but six million  children overwhelmingly latino and  african-american children will basically  be condemned by zip code to failing  schools gloria you are a leading  democrat you're still a democrat  and i've always wondered this this one  question because we saw it in the white  house when cdc said it is safe for kids  to go back to school but then there was  an email that went out and the teachers  unions changed that and jinsaki the  press secretary said no actually it's  not right so what happens behind closed  doors  with the teachers union do they send  demands out and legislators are expected  to go along with it or they won't get  endorsements or they will fund their  opponents what happens  money talks  and the politicians walk that's really  what happens uh cta is the most powerful  political force in california it  contributes more to a political war  chest than oil pharmaceuticals  gas combined  and these are not your everyday teachers  in a classroom and we have seen fights  that have gone all the way to the  supreme court to try to break free of  those mandatory union jews that  basically pay for candidates and issues  that rank and file teachers don't  support so it really is the power of  money that basically has become a very  sour milk in reproducing inequality in  california and really much across the  nation as well and that's what this  recall to me was about a chance to break  this system and i found no stronger  voice than larry elder who actually has  survived that and is an eloquent speaker  on the need for school choice thank you  gloria i appreciate you joining the  program i know that the democratic  machine is going to be after you thank  you so much

